WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:38.820
A day in November, Miss Stacy gathered
her students above 13 years old by the lake

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.500
to talk about their future lives.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.120
After that, on their way home...

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.670
The woods were lovely
with their Autumn colors

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.170
but they're also beautiful with fallen leaves.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:59.300
Look, Diana. The ferns and the satin leaves
and the crackerberries have gone to sleep,

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.970
just as if somebody had tucked them away
until spring under a blanket of leaves.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:13.980
I think it was a little gray fairy
with a rainbow scarf who did it.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.400
Anne, you know there is no such things as fairies.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.800
Oh, Diana. That's why we should
use our imagination.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.650
But we are so much older
than we used to be

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.420
that it isn't becoming
to talk of childish matters.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.510
Oh, please don't say that imagination is childish.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.950
It is very important to cultivate our imagination.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.330
It is what Miss Stacy says, isn't it?

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.950
Miss Stacy also said today

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:43.390
that we couldn't be too careful what
habits and ideals we acquired in our teens,

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.210
because by the time we were
twenty our characters would be developed.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.450
If you want to imagine,

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.300
then you should imagine
something useful for your future.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.810
For example...

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.300
I know.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.620
About marriage.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:57.940
Marriage?

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:58.870
That's right.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.330
Diana!

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.030
Didn't we promise each other
that we would never marry

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:10.260
but be nice old maids and
live together forever?

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.440
That's because Ruby is always talking of
nothing but young men. So I...

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.230
I didn't quite made up my mind though.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.880
Because I think that
perhaps it would be nobler,

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.040
to marry some wild,
dashing, wicked young man and reform him.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.050
Oh! That's great, Diana.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.500
It would be a meaningful marriage.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.280
You really think so?

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.400
Of course I do!

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.390
You have been thinking seriously
about you future, haven't you?

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:40.640
But...

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.230
...I feel so lonely.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:49.690
I had decided to give up
marriage forever for our friendship.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.250
But, Anne...

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.850
Didn't you say the other day,

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:56.680
that you wanted to marry
a missionary and go see the world?

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.550
That was only a dream.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.160
How would I know where to find
an ideal missionary in this world?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.400
You're right.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:07.520
Also,

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.010
you cannot be sure that
you will meet your ideal bad boy.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.460
So like I though,

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.000
it would be better for us
to stay single until we meet them.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:16.670
But...

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.560
Do you intend to marry
even if you don't find your ideal?

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.220
What?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.400
That's not what I intend, but...

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.190
Oh, Diana,

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.160
you're the same as Ruby.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.280
Jane told me the other
day after the prayer meeting,

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.430
that you let Moody Spurgeon accompany
you, and you seemed happy about it.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.360
Oh! And you believed that, Anne?

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.100
Of course.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:44.030
Today I saw both of you
chatting and laughing together.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.080
Then I tell you right now!

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.940
I do not care for Moody,

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.940
but can't I be happy
just because he sent me home?

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.770
See?

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.040
You never wanted to be
single with me from the start.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.990
You prefer boys over
our friendship, isn't that right, Diana?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.770
Why are you saying
those horrible things to me?

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.700
I really treasure our friendship.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.040
But, Anne,

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.140
you refuse to talk
to Gilbert because of a silly thing,

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:13.910
and now, you want to stop
me from talking to others boys?

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.490
This is the end of our friendship!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.000
Anne!

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:47.770
I'm home.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.850
Matthew.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.170
Jerry.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.920
Matthew is not back yet.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.130
Anne.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.020
Well, since Matthew is
not here, I'll just leave this here.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.760
Did you eat the apples that were on the barrel?

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:33.290
What?

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:33.900
Yes...

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.650
Those apples were yours?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.660
I'm sorry.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.530
Oh, Lord, please forgive me.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:43.400
I never expected her to eat those apples!

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:44.130
What?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:46.790
Those apples were poisonous!

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.530
I've poisoned those apples for the rats!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.180
I've seen many rats since
the day I started to work here,

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.840
and I wanted to stop them from breeding!

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:03.040
The quantity is enough to
kill a dozen of you instantly!

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:07.800
Anne!

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.100
Marilla!

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:33.570
Is anyone home?

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.300
I'm so scared!
I don't want to die alone.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:42.680
I don't want to die!

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.720
But I am going to die for sure.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:51.850
Diana!

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:54.710
I can't die while we're still angry at each other.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.620
It was my fault, I have to apologise to her.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:59.980
I will apologise to her right away.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.430
But what if I die on the way?

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:09.660
To die out there alone in the dark,
oh, that would be dreadful.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:26.590
When someone arrives,
they will only find my stiff cold body.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:32.090
Oh, I just want to be
able to bid farewell to everyone.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:37.980
All I did was eat some delicious-looking apples.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.330
It isn't fair!

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.750
I don't deserve to die!

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:51.360
I don't want to die!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.900
Now it's not the time to cry.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.630
I must have courage.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:09.340
You can't bring shame to the Shirleys
and the Cuthberts, Anne Shirley!

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:20.440
Right, If I have to die,
then I should die peacefully in my bed.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.140
How long it will take until I die?

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:57.570
Jerry said I will die instantly
after eating the apples, but...

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.040
...how long it will be?

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:04.640
How much time is an instant?

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.950
Will it hurt to die?

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.350
I'm sure poison does hurt awfully.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:13.540
Oh, and just a little while ago I was so happy!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:18.150
At least let me have some time to
write my last words to Marilla and Matthew.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:19.990
And also to Diana.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:25.600
Otherwise, Diana will feel remorseful
after hearing about my death.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:31.790
I shouldn't have said that to her,
but she hurt my feelings too.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.430
But do I have enough time?

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.270
Why are my hands so cold?

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:40.730
Maybe I'm already dying?

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:43.160
Is my face turning black?

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:51.070
I'm as pale as the dead already.
This is a dying face without doubt!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.020
I don't want to die, but since I have to

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:01.820
I'll die with dignity so I don't
embarrass Green Gables!

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.950
Dear Diana,

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:12.340
I am going to die.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:17.050
I have been poisoned by an
apple Jerry had put for rats.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:23.870
I will never see you again,
but I want to tell you I love you.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:28.730
I regret deeply what I said to you earlier.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.280
You were right.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:37.140
I am writing this to tell you that you are not
to feel bad over what you said.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:41.640
Oh, Diana, please forgive me.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:48.540
I do not feel sick yet but I don't know
what the symptoms of poisoning are.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:59.610
Jerry said there was enough to kill
a dozen of me, so I can't have long to live.

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:08.910
I think I feel a pain in my stomach now
so I guess that the end draws near.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:09.920
Farewell,

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:15.920
and remember her who died so young.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:17.840
Your own devoted,

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.570
Anne Shirley.

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:23.800
Diana...

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:41.830
Anne.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.180
What is going on?
The lights aren't even on.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.740
There's no fire in the stove.
What is she doing...

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.510
I'm dying.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:52.820
What did you say?

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:57.890
I ate some apples
Jerry buote had poisoned for rats.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:03.130
I have only a few minutes to live, Marilla.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.370
Anne, is this some play-acting of yours?

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.440
No it's not, Marilla.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:15.280
Do you suppose a dying person
would be play-acting?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:20.690
Would you please read this after I die?
And this one is for Diana.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:28.100
Don't let anyone see me after I'm dead.
I don't want them to see my black face.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:32.150
Anne, how long ago is it
since you ate that apple?

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:34.280
About an hour.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:41.230
If you'd eaten a poisoned apple an
hour ago you'd be dead or sick by now.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:49.160
But I felt a pain in my stomach.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:56.280
What's the matter?
Why is the lamp turn off?

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:59.140
Matthew, where is Jerry buote?

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:04.210
Well now, I think he is in the barn.
Or maybe on the way home.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.230
How did he look?

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:09.250
Well now, the same as usual.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.780
Anne, come with me.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.480
Jerry! Jerry buote!

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.180
What is it?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.360
Did you cause Anne to
eat some poisoned apples?

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.080
What?

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.000
Oh, that...

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:31.710
No way.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.390
That was just a joke.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.670
Just as I thought.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.510
You shouldn't scare girls with poison.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:41.780
No, I...

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:46.240
I wanted to eat those
apples during my break,

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:48.010
so I... well...

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.430
How dare you play tricks on me, Jerry Buote!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:51.580
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:56.580
But you started to run so suddenly
that I couldn't tell you the truth.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.510
But I thought you would
figure out it was only a joke.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.160
Jerry Buote, you are going to pay!

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.070
I won't forgive you!

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:03.200
I'm sorry, Anne!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.110
Wait!

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:05.120
Stop that, Anne!

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.290
You shouldn't be so greedy.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:08.330
Jerry Buote! Stop!

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:08.600
Alright! I'm sorry!
Jerry Buote! Stop!

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:09.380
Alright! I'm sorry!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:10.010
Wait!

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:11.810
Forgive me!

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:22.200
But Marilla, I did have a pain in my stomach.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.780
Of course.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:28.410
After spending a hour thinking you are dying,
anyone would get a stomach ache.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:30.100
Oh, yes.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.000
With all this I almost forgot.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.120
Anne, I saw Miss Stacy today.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:39.250
She was coming here to tell us something.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:41.610
Anne, are you listening?

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.540
Yes. What did she want?

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.520
You don't seem so interested to know.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.200
She was talking about you.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.990
About me?

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:54.160
That's right.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:55.190
Oh!

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.510
I know what she was saying.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:01.060
I meant to tell you, Marilla,

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.970
honestly I did, but I forgot.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.280
Miss Stacy caught me reading
Ben Hur in school yesterday afternoon

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.340
when I should have been
studying my Canadian history.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:12.130
I was reading it at dinner hour,

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.450
and I had just got to the
chariot race when school went in.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.820
I was simply
wild to know how it turned out.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.200
Although I felt sure Ben Hur must win,

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:26.690
because it wouldn't be
poetical justice if he didn't.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.710
So I spread the
history open on my desk lid

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.830
and then tucked Ben Hur
between the desk and my knee.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:37.070
I just looked as if I were
studying Canadian history, you know,

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:40.220
while all the while I was reveling in Ben Hur.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.210
I was so interested in it

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:48.090
that I never noticed
Miss Stacy coming down the aisle.

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:50.680
Until all at once I just looked up

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:54.220
and there she
was looking down at me, so reproachful-like.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:57.770
I can't tell you how ashamed I felt.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:01.460
Especially when I heard Josie Pye giggling.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:05.730
Miss Stacy took Ben Hur away,

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.190
but she never said a word then.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:13.400
She kept me in at
recess and talked to me.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.690
And I promised
I'd never do such a thing again.

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:20.980
And I offered to do penance by never
looking at Ben Hur for a whole week,

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.890
not even to see how the chariot race turned out.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:31.400
But Miss Stacy said she wouldn't
require that, and she forgave me freely.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:37.080
So I think it wasn't very kind of her
to come up here to you about it after all.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.890
Miss Stacy never
mentioned such a thing to me, Anne.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:44.010
Its only your guilty conscience
that's the matter with you.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:48.290
You have no business to be
taking storybooks to school.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.740
You read too many novels anyhow.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:57.020
Oh, how can you call Ben Hur a novel
when it's really such a religious book?

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.870
If it's not a novel, then what is it?

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:04.720
Of course it's a little too exciting to be
proper reading for Sunday

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:08.040
and I only read it on weekdays.
And I ne...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:12.930
Well, I think I'll go to bed.
My eyes and ears are getting tired.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:17.430
I see plainly that you don't want
to hear what Miss Stacy had to say.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:23.260
You're more interested in the sound of
your own tongue than in anything else.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:26.750
Oh, indeed, Marilla, I do want to hear it!

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:31.570
I won't say another word. Not one.
Please tell me, Marilla.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:37.910
Miss Stacy wants to organize a
class among her advanced students

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.750
who mean to study for the entrance
examination into Queen's.

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:44.960
She intends to give them extra lessons
for an hour after school.

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:51.410
And she came to ask Matthew and me
if we would like to have you join it.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:54.340
What do you think, Anne?

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:58.140
Would you like to go to Queen's
and pass for a teacher?

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:02.180
Oh, Marilla!
It's been the dream of my life!

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:07.880
That is, for the last six months, ever since
Ruby and Jane began to talk about it.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.740
I'm sure Diana and Josie Pye are going too.

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:16.740
But I didn't say anything about it, because
I supposed it would be perfectly useless.

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:19.250
I'd love to be a teacher.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:22.940
But... won't it be dreadfully expensive?

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:28.440
Mr. Andrews says it cost him one hundred
and fifty dollars to put Prissy through,

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:31.780
and Prissy wasn't a dunce in geometry.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:35.180
You needn't worry about that, Anne.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:39.260
When Matthew and I took you to bring up

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:44.660
we resolved we would do the best we could
for you and give you a good education.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.880
Isn't that right, Matthew?

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:50.960
Yes, that's right.
Don't worry, Anne.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:21:01.070
I believe in a girl being fitted to earn her
own living whether she ever has to or not.

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:06.450
You'll always have a home at Green Gables
as long as Matthew and I are here,

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:12.030
but nobody knows what is going
to happen in this uncertain world,

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:15.150
and it's just as well to be prepared.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:20.030
So you can join the Queen's class
if you like, Anne.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:22.240
Ma-Marilla...!

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:24.400
Oh, Marilla, thank you.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:26.280
This looks like a dream!

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:29.670
No, it's not a dream!
I'll study as hard as I can!

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:31.300
Thank you, Marilla!

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.300
Matthew, thank you!

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:38.190
I will never forget about this,

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.810
and I'll study as hard as I can and do
my very best to be a credit to you both.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.650
I warn you not to expect much in geometry,

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:50.630
but I think I can hold my own in
anything else if I work hard.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:54.100
Of course.
I dare say you'll get along well enough.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:59.580
Miss Stacy says you are bright and diligent.

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:01.700
Really? She said that?

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:02.480
But, Anne,

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.960
you needn't rush to any extreme
of killing yourself over your books.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:09.370
You won't be ready to
try the Entrance for a year and a half yet.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:13.610
But it's well to begin in time
and be thoroughly grounded,

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:16.060
Miss Stacy says.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.730
I shall take more interest
than ever in my studies now,

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:22.390
because I have a purpose in life.

00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:24.540
Mr. Allan says

00:22:25.140 --> 00:22:30.050
everybody should have a
purpose in life and pursue it faithfully.

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:36.550
Only he says we must first
make sure that it is a worthy purpose.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:41.230
I would call it a worthy purpose to want to be
a teacher like Miss Stacy, wouldn't you, Marilla?

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:42.990
I think it's a very noble profession.

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:47.940
Just a while ago I thought I
would die by eating poisoned apples,

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:50.350
but since I am still alive,
I feel I can do anything.

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:53.030
That's why no matter how hard it will be,

00:22:53.030 --> 00:22:55.180
I will get into the Queen's Academy.

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:58.070
What is this about dying?

00:22:58.380 --> 00:22:59.490
About that, Matthew...

00:22:59.490 --> 00:23:01.340
Oh! Don't say it, Marilla!

00:23:01.700 --> 00:23:04.290
Right! I'm going to tell the news to Diana.

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:06.410
I had a quarrel with her today.

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:10.460
We have been talking about our futures.

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:13.100
But we have different opinions.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:15.120
Today it was all my fault.

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:16.960
Then, I'll be back soon.

00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:19.250
It's late, tell her tomorrow.

00:23:19.340 --> 00:23:21.020
Do you know what time it is?

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:23.800
You're right.

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:25.630
I'll tell her tomorrow.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:29.530
Many unpleasant things
happened today, but ended well.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:32.100
Good night, Matthew, Marilla!

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:33.780
Good night, Anne.

00:23:33.900 --> 00:23:35.000
Good night.

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:55.780
Diana, I know you will be happy for me.

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:19.090
The Queens class is formed

00:24:19.090 --> 00:24:23.360
but Diana didn't join
and it was a big blow to Anne.

00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:26.300
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:28.780
Diana and the Students for Queens Class

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:29.780
Please watch!
